* t57linea.a -- CONF68K test t57: a line-A handler installed with F$STrap* catches an A-line instruction.** Claim (DOCS/claims.md): the exceptions a user program may catch with* F$STrap include the line 1010 and line 1111 emulator traps -- vectors 10* and 11 -- alongside bus error, address error, illegal instruction, zero* divide, CHK, TRAPV and privilege violation. v2.4 TRM page 1-60.** An A-line opcode raises vector 10 on every 68k: the 1010 range is reserved* and no processor implements it, which is why it is the classic hook for a* run-time to extend the instruction set. A program installing a handler for* it is asking to be told rather than killed.** NOT line-F, deliberately. os9exec emulates a 68020 WITH a 68881, so an* F-line word in the coprocessor-1 range ($F2xx) is a legal FPU instruction* and is executed, not trapped -- measured 2026-09-12, where it consumed the* following word as its extension and ran the PC into this table. A line-F* test would have to use an unimplemented coprocessor id, and would assert* something about the FPU model rather than about F$STrap.** The test installs a handler for T_LINEA, executes dc.w $A000, and reports* from the handler. obs is 0 when the* handler ran, and the test cannot report at all if the exception kills the* process instead -- a MISSING result line, exactly as t50 behaves when* MOVE from SR traps. tools/conformance.sh names the missing test.*Prgrm set 1Objct set 1ReEnt set $80Type_Lang set (Prgrm<<8)+ObjctAttr_Rev set (ReEnt<<8)+1*FSTrap set $0ET_LINEA set $28RPC set $42*EXPECT set 0* psect t57linea,Type_Lang,Attr_Rev,0,2048,startstart moveq #0,d0 movea.l d0,a0 lea exctbl(pc),a1 trap #0 dc.w FSTrap bcs.w setuperr moveq #9,d6 dc.w $A000 bra.w isfail*exctbl dc.w T_LINEA,handler-*-4 dc.w -1*handler moveq #0,d6 cmpi.l #EXPECT,d6 beq.w ispass bra.w isfail* use verdict.i use report.i*idstr dc.b "RESULT t57 ",0passtr dc.b "PASS",0failstr dc.b "FAIL",0errstr dc.b "ERROR",0obsstr dc.b "  obs=",0expstr dc.b " exp=",0descstr dc.b "  an F$STrap handler catches a line-A exception",0 ends